    "result_text": "All 264 tests pass. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented optional, unique email support for owner creation on `POST /api/owners`:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an optional `email` string field to the `OwnerFields` schema (inherited by both `OwnerFieldsDto` and `OwnerDto`, and auto-wired through the MapStruct `OwnerMapper`).\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `email` column mapping with getter/setter.\n\n3. **DB schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added a nullable `email VARCHAR(255)` column to the `owners` table.\n\n4. **`hsqldb/data.sql`** \u2014 the seed inserts used positional `INSERT INTO owners VALUES (...)`; I gave them an explicit column list so the new column doesn't break them (the other dialects already used explicit column lists).\n\n5. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 added an `emailAlreadyExists` check that returns `409 CONFLICT` when a supplied email is already used by another owner. A missing/blank email is ignored, so it never conflicts and is stored/returned as-is.\n\nThe new `Cp04Tests` (reject duplicate email \u2192 409, allow missing email, store & return email) all pass, along with the full 264-test suite.",
